provenance.prompt:
Create one original transparent RGBA sprite sheet for Paprika's JAMVERSE '96 reverse layup. Paprika is a REAL TINY FOUR-FOOTED KIT FOX: a horizontal compact wild-fox body, russet-orange fur, cream-white muzzle/chest/underside, huge triangular ears, bright expressive fox eyes, long pointed muzzle, big bushy tail with a pale tip, and fitted purple-and-gold sports vest. Preserve her same small natural fox proportions in all drawings. She stays on four animal legs with fox paws in every pose; never humanoid, never upright like a person, no human arms or hands, shoes, shorts, cloak, or canine species other than a small kit fox. Match polished richly shaded 1990s arcade pixel-sprite art with crisp readable outlines.

Draw EXACTLY eight separate complete right-facing three-quarter full-body fox poses in a strict 4-column by 2-row grid, row-major. Every pose is independently drawn, anatomically plausible, the same scale and camera angle, with generous true-transparent gutters. Keep ears, muzzle, four paws, and full pale-tipped tail inside each cell. No contact between figures, overlap, crop, duplicates, grid marks, panels, or borders.

This is a reverse-side layup. The game draws the basketball separately; never draw a ball.
Pose order is tied to the existing JAMVERSE runtime: frame 4 (zero-based pose 4, fifth cell) is the high reverse-side peak and preparation; Paprika has NOT released yet and keeps the invisible ball close to her muzzle. Frame 5 (zero-based pose 5, sixth cell) is the actual RELEASE pose at tick 12: a distinct nose-flick over her shoulder with the near fox forepaw reaching behind the turned head toward the reverse-side release lane. Do not move the release to another cell.
0) low quadruped approach along the baseline;
1) gather with muzzle close to the invisible ball, forepaws tucked, hind legs preparing;
2) compact four-paw plant and crouch, beginning a backward shoulder/head turn;
3) leap across the lane, body rotating naturally but still horizontal and fox-like;
4) high airborne peak, shoulders and muzzle turned over her shoulder, forepaw cocked behind the head, holding the invisible ball at the muzzle before release;
5) RELEASE at peak: sharp upward-backward muzzle flick and extended near forepaw, all paws still animal paws, ears and tail readable;
6) follow through and descend beyond the hoop with forepaws reaching down first;
7) land on all four paws and recover balanced, still facing right.

Transparent background. No basketball or ball-like object, hoop, rim, net, court, floor, shadow, humans, opponents, extra animals, lettering, numerals, logos, background, glow, or equipment.
